'''Abberath's Fury''' is a [[trigger]]ed [[spell]] that deals [[fire damage]] in an area. Abberath's Fury is granted by {{il|Abberath's Hooves}}.

==Mechanics==
Abberath's Fury can be supported by applicable [[support gem]]s socketed in Abberath's Hooves; it is not necessary that the sockets be [[link]]ed. Abberath's Fury is not a skill gem, therefore it cannot be supported by {{il|Empower Support}}, {{il|Enhance Support}}, or {{il|Enlighten Support}}.

==Skill Functions and Interactions==
'''Triggering:''' Abberath's Fury's damage applies each time the character takes a step. Modifiers to [[movement speed]] will increase the frequency at which the damage occurs.

There is a limit to this effect at around +160% movement speed. If a player exceeds this limit, the damage frequency is dramatically reduced and the spell sometimes skips a cast. This is possibly due to how "steps" are implemented.

This spell is only triggered when the item granting it is equipped. Abberath's Fury does not trigger every time you take a step. This prevents Abberath's Fury from triggering around your Triggerbots since the spell is not triggering repeatedly. You do however still take the 35% less damage penalty from the Perfect Crime ascendancy point as Abberath's Fury is a triggered spell.

Both versions of Abberath's Fury can be used simultaneously from {{il|Abberath's Hooves}} and [[Polytheist]]'s [[Devout of Abberath]]. The support gems on the boots will not support the skill from the ascendancy passive.

'''Cast Speed:''' Modifiers to [[cast speed]] have no effect on the spell's cast rate or frequency, despite changing the tooltip. Sometimes the spell will lag behind the player's movement after a negative cast speed modifier is applied. This usually disappears after entering a new area.

'''Movement skills:''' The movement skills will not trigger explosions. The only exception is {{il|Shield Charge}}, as player is technically still walking but at a greatly increased speed.

==Acquisition==
This skill can only be gained indirectly through certain items or modifiers:

* {{il|Abberath's Hooves}}: {{c|mod|Triggers Level 7 Abberath's Fury when Equipped}}
* [[Devout of Abberath]] ([[Legacy of Phrecia]]): {{c|mod|Triggers Level 20 Abberath's Fury}}

